{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"282a039b-60e6-4f58-acf1-7b3263cbd098","status":"SUCCESS","response":"A standalone pure-Python `slugify` implementation and corresponding unit test suite are in place and verified.\n\n### Implementation Summary\n\n1. **[slugify.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/slugify.py)**:\n   - Function: [`slugify(value, allow_unicode=False, separator=\"-\")`](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/slugify.py#L5-L41)\n   - Uses standard library modules `re` and `unicodedata` (pure Python, zero third-party dependencies).\n   - Handles Unicode transliteration to ASCII (e.g. converting accents like `Crème brûlée` to `creme-brulee`), with an optional `allow_unicode=True` mode.\n   - Cleans disallowable symbols, collapses repeated delimiters and whitespace, trims leading/trailing delimiters, and supports custom separator characters.\n\n2. **[test_slugify.py](file:///C:/Users/jayde/.gemini/AI-Lab/src/test_slugify.py)**:\n   - Uses Python's built-in `unittest` framework covering:\n     - Basic ASCII conversion and case normalization (`Hello World` \u0026rarr; `hello-world`).\n     - Custom separators (e.g. `_`).\n     - Multiple consecutive spaces, hyphens, and leading/trailing whitespace.\n     - Stripping punctuation and special symbols (`#`, `@`, etc.).\n     - Accented character transliteration (NFKD decomposition).\n     - Unicode preservation mode (`allow_unicode=True`).\n     - Edge cases: empty strings, whitespace-only strings, and non-string types.\n\n### Test Execution\n```bash\npython -m unittest src/test_slugify.py\nRan 8 tests in 0.000s - OK\n```\n","duration_seconds":22.6257941,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":74636,"output_tokens":918,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":122505,"total_tokens":75554}}}
